_of":"H1FY26"},"management_tone":{"title":"Management quality / tone","body":"Highly confident, visionary, transparent; emphasized ecosystem lock-in, recurring revenue, and generational shift in textile printing; strong focus on long-term value creation","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"risks":{"title":"Risks & watch-items","body":"Dependence on machine sales volatility; potential competition from Chinese OEMs; ink quality lock-in risk if third-party inks gain warranty acceptance; subsidy policy changes","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"non_obvious":{"title":"Non-obvious takeaways","body":"Customer retention is not just about price — it's warranty voidance if non-True Colors ink is used, creating de facto exclusivity; 560 active machines already in field generating daily recurring revenue; 7-8% self-consumption of paper is strategic to ensure quality control and supply chain resilience","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"challenges":{"title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers","body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| — | — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"}}}